> [!NOTE]
> **DISCLAIMER:** This comment was written by an LLM, Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`, 1M context), posting on behalf of @HeartSaVioR.

Fixed in [e8fcf1b7ad7](https://github.com/apache/spark/commit/e8fcf1b7ad728f342ba8d9e22005a97c65d26c46). The per-entry overhead is now 168 bytes, taken from the objects each entry holds:
- Guava's entry with its links: 64 bytes, or 48 without a TTL;
- the weighted value reference: 24;
- the hash-table slot and spare room: 8;
- the key's UnsafeRow, 40, and its array header, 16;
- the header of the rows array: 16.

JOL on JDK 21 measures Guava's objects at 88 to 90 bytes per entry with a TTL, which this covers.

